+{"citation_id": "cite-20261025-001", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "When a feature is added to a slice or taken out of it after its plan exists, what must the plan play do with the stories of that slice?", "answer": "When a feature comes into the slice, the plan play adds one story for it, so that each feature of the slice has a story; it makes no second story for a feature that has one; and nothing goes to the tracker before the product owner's yes. What it does with the story of a feature that goes out is not set by the model: the product owner says.", "decided_by": "propose-answers (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:38:31Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what the plan play does when the slice changes after a plan exists", "found": "a second run makes no copies, nothing goes to the tracker before the yes, and the changed-slice rule is not set yet", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 20, "end": 22, "fingerprint": "sha256:324b2a6a4915a79c736df1bfad097680a096e52cb98e85b744965c7c5466b724", "text": "- A second run finds the plan, the epic and the stories that exist, and makes no copies.\n- Nothing goes to the tracker before the product owner's yes.\n- Thin: what the play does when the slice changes after a plan exists is not set yet.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 17, "end": 25, "text": "- The play runs after /shape-slice, on its own, and needs the slice to exist.\n- Each story carries the goal, the limits, the expectations and the Context guidance from its feature's ICE and its capability's ICE.\n- The play never writes a failure or recovery condition. The slice's hidden file belongs to /shape-slice (decision 6).\n- A second run finds the plan, the epic and the stories that exist, and makes no copies.\n- Nothing goes to the tracker before the product owner's yes.\n- Thin: what the play does when the slice changes after a plan exists is not set yet.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given a slice with three features, when the product owner runs /shape-plan and types yes, then one plan file, one epic and three stories exist."}}}, {"asked": "whether each feature of the slice must have one story", "found": "fails if a feature has no story or a second story is made for one feature", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 44, "end": 46, "fingerprint": "sha256:6d32cce6e8cb5a000490f23ce2b15407e86f9a5be47349137afb58551a0b0fb0", "text": "- Fails if: a feature of the slice has no story.\n- Fails if: a story or the plan file holds a failure condition or a recovery condition.\n- Fails if: a second run makes a second epic for the slice or a second story for one feature.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 41, "end": 48, "text": "- Limit: Write only the plan file, the epic and the stories. Never a failure condition, a recovery condition, the hidden file's failure or recovery lines, or the eval.\n- Limit: Each story holds the goal, the limits, the expectations and the Context guidance from its feature's ICE and that feature's capability's ICE.\n- Limit: Nothing goes to the tracker before the product owner's yes.\n- Fails if: a feature of the slice has no story.\n- Fails if: a story or the plan file holds a failure condition or a recovery condition.\n- Fails if: a second run makes a second epic for the slice or a second story for one feature.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who runs and tracks the plan, and the build play, which reads the stories; reads the slice from the spine and the ICE of each feature and its capability; writes .garura/project/plans/ and the tracker; out are the slice, the hidden file, the eval and the build. Not built yet (#818).\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code after /shape-slice and finds the plan file, one epic and one story for each feature, with no failure line in any story."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261025-002", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In what form must the eval play write the eval of a slice, so that a person can run it from the outside?", "answer": "The eval is written in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). For each goal and expectation of the stories, and each failure condition of the slice's hidden file, it holds one check run from the outside on the slice's surface (for Garura often a run of the play on a test project), or a note that it cannot be tested yet. The layout of the file itself is not set by the model: the product owner says.", "decided_by": "propose-answers (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:38:31Z", "trace": [{"asked": "where the eval goes and whether its format is set", "found": "one eval in the plan's evals folder; the format is not set yet", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 11, "end": 13, "fingerprint": "sha256:b93cde941566d22f8052938724f9ccd125579b6b69cb933287c3d514fd7bf65d", "text": "- Out: one eval for the business intent in `.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/`.\n- Out (when needed): a handoff plan, which never names a failure condition, its id or its check.\n- Thin: the format of the eval and of the handoff plan is not set yet.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 16, "text": "## Inputs / Outputs\n- In: the epic of the slice, with its feature-to-story map, and its stories. The map joins each hidden-file entry (by its feature) to its story (ontology v11, Q36).\n- In: the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md) from the plan's evals folder.\n- Out: one eval for the business intent in `.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/`.\n- Out (when needed): a handoff plan, which never names a failure condition, its id or its check.\n- Thin: the format of the eval and of the handoff plan is not set yet.\n\n## Rules & behavior\n- The play runs after /shape-plan, on its own."}}}, {"asked": "how the eval checks", "found": "from the outside on the slice's surface, often a play on a test project; says when it cannot test a line yet", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 18, "end": 20, "fingerprint": "sha256:a328b9382c241adfa7d50c22485235986fdbe38e98a1f8562ebeb8df3e7b2c5c", "text": "- The eval checks from the outside, on the slice's surface. For Garura that surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project.\n- The running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (`guides/<slug>.md`).\n- When the eval cannot test a goal, an expectation or a failure condition yet, it says so.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 15, "end": 23, "text": "## Rules & behavior\n- The play runs after /shape-plan, on its own.\n- It reads only the epic, its stories and the hidden file. It never reads an ICE page, the usage guide or the code.\n- The eval checks from the outside, on the slice's surface. For Garura that surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project.\n- The running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (`guides/<slug>.md`).\n- When the eval cannot test a goal, an expectation or a failure condition yet, it says so.\n- Until eval encryption (#828) exists, only a read rule keeps builders out of the evals folder.\n\n## Acceptance criteria"}}}, {"asked": "what each check must cover", "found": "each goal, expectation and failure condition has a check or a note that it cannot be tested yet", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 25, "end": 25, "fingerprint": "sha256:704c849e5b5d54f153dd6bb385408aa60295d4490f8bf82def0ee24f2b87850e", "text": "- Given the eval, when a person reads it, then each goal and expectation of the stories, and each failure condition of the hidden file, has a check or a note that it cannot be tested yet.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 22, "end": 28, "text": "\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given a plan with an epic and its stories, when the product owner runs /shape-eval, then the eval is in the plan's evals folder.\n- Given the eval, when a person reads it, then each goal and expectation of the stories, and each failure condition of the hidden file, has a check or a note that it cannot be tested yet.\n- Given the build plays, when a person reads their inputs, then none names the evals folder.\n\n## Out of scope"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261025-003", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "May the slice be shaped when the ICE of its features is still thin?", "answer": "Yes. The slice feature's page says the play proposes a thin ICE, marks it thin, warns the person and never sends them back; the ready check calls a part with gaps like that partly ready, and work goes on.", "decided_by": "propose-answers (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:38:31Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what the play does for a part with no ICE", "found": "it proposes a thin ICE, marks it thin, warns the person and never sends them back", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-slice/fn-795/feature.md", "start": 22, "end": 22, "fingerprint": "sha256:3c22d8fd01578e664b4efcc26a9eeb6b062b0819060b93c9cb1ce3b028206988", "text": "- For a part the slice needs that has no ICE, the play proposes a thin ICE (at least a goal, a limit and one \"Fails if\" line, one Context line and one Expectation line), marks it thin and warns the person; it never sends the person back (ontology v11, ICE; ADR 052 §5). Not built yet (#842).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 19, "end": 25, "text": "- When a slice already serves the intent, the play uses that slice again and makes no new one.\n- The confirmation shows the slice only: what you run, who tests it, the features under each capability, and what is left out (decision 4).\n- Nothing is kept before the person types yes. A stop undoes every write.\n- For a part the slice needs that has no ICE, the play proposes a thin ICE (at least a goal, a limit and one \"Fails if\" line, one Context line and one Expectation line), marks it thin and warns the person; it never sends the person back (ontology v11, ICE; ADR 052 §5). Not built yet (#842).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given an intent with no slice, when the product owner runs /shape-slice for it and types yes, then the spine holds one slice that serves the intent."}}}, {"asked": "whether a part with gaps may go forward", "found": "partly ready: the ICE goes forward and work starts", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/capabilities/cap-723/capability.md", "start": 11, "end": 11, "fingerprint": "sha256:be09240c068fb61293ab0aa37ad8033b7a3129d168c683aba96556017726f7e6", "text": "  - Partly ready: it is ready, but the check found gaps that do not stop work, such as no domain or an ICE with no context yet. The ICE goes forward, and work starts. The check lists each gap to fix later. (Our proposal: what counts as a gap is not yet agreed.)", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 14, "text": "  - A capability or feature can need another capability or feature. \"Needs\" means the other one must be done first. Work items (Epic, Story, Spike, Chore, Bug) never need anything.\n- How we will know: a ready check gives one answer for each capability and feature. It reads the links, the needs and the status of each part, and applies the rules above.\n  - Ready: it serves a confirmed business intent, and everything it needs is done. The agent intent (ICE) goes forward, and work starts.\n  - Partly ready: it is ready, but the check found gaps that do not stop work, such as no domain or an ICE with no context yet. The ICE goes forward, and work starts. The check lists each gap to fix later. (Our proposal: what counts as a gap is not yet agreed.)\n  - Not ready: it serves no confirmed business intent, or something it needs is not done. The ICE does not go forward, and work stops until the cause is fixed. The page itself is kept.\n\n## Boundary (In / Out / Never)"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261025-004", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Does each of the three shaping plays end at its own confirmation by the product owner?", "answer": "Yes. The confirmed intent's proof says each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner; the loop's one approval (#796) is out of scope.", "decided_by": "propose-answers (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:38:31Z", "trace": [{"asked": "how each shaping play ends", "found": "each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 14, "end": 14, "fingerprint": "sha256:63c741c28021d439129517392964958d69cd212e07c8f86aca5377888f87c90e", "text": "- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 11, "end": 17, "text": "- The design has a slice that one person can test end to end on one surface, with the features it needs in build order.\n- The design has a plan that a person can run and track: the plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature.\n- The design has an eval that tests, from the outside, if the business intent is met.\n- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.\n- A play runs each step. No step is done by hand.\n- The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.\n"}}}, {"asked": "whether the loop's one approval is in scope", "found": "the loop and its one approval (#796) are out of scope", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-slice/fn-795/feature.md", "start": 34, "end": 34, "fingerprint": "sha256:2d2e9f1dc7a309dcb61db8e63fbff6d5ea46930b2afd39d9fe7ee8b7d7e57679", "text": "- The loop that runs the three plays and its one approval (#796, decision 1).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 31, "end": 37, "text": "## Out of scope\n- The plan file, the epic and the stories. /shape-plan writes them (fn-818).\n- The eval. /shape-eval writes it (fn-798).\n- The loop that runs the three plays and its one approval (#796, decision 1).\n- Eval encryption (#828) and the author-slice skill (#838), decision 3.\n\n> Thin ICE: proposed by /shape-slice for bi-788 (#844, decision 7); deepen with /discover-capabilities."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261025-005", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Where must the eval of a slice be kept so that no builder can read it?", "answer": "In the plan's evals folder, .garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/, which no builder, building skill or context sub-agent reads; until eval encryption (#828) only a read rule keeps builders out.", "decided_by": "propose-answers (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:38:32Z", "trace": [{"asked": "where the eval is kept and who may read it", "found": "only in the plan's evals folder; fails if a builder can read it; until #828 only a read rule keeps builders out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md", "start": 19, "end": 23, "fingerprint": "sha256:eebe1671a093838fbde714fd9c228c7f6872471e8b74a03ba3279d81ac812b36", "text": "- Limit: Write only in the plan's evals folder: .garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/.\n- Fails if: a builder can read the eval.\n- Fails if: the eval checks something the business intent does not ask for.\n- Fails if: the eval play reads an ICE page, the usage guide or the code.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who wants proof that the intent is met, and the running eval after the build; reads what /shape-plan and /shape-slice wrote; until #828 only a read rule keeps the folder from builders; out are running the eval and encrypting it.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 16, "end": 24, "text": "## Agent intent (ICE)\n- Goal: Each slice has one eval that says, from the outside, if its business intent is met on the slice's surface.\n- Limit: Read the epic, its stories and the hidden file; never an ICE page, the usage guide or the code.\n- Limit: Write only in the plan's evals folder: .garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/.\n- Fails if: a builder can read the eval.\n- Fails if: the eval checks something the business intent does not ask for.\n- Fails if: the eval play reads an ICE page, the usage guide or the code.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who wants proof that the intent is met, and the running eval after the build; reads what /shape-plan and /shape-slice wrote; until #828 only a read rule keeps the folder from builders; out are running the eval and encrypting it.\n- Checked by: /shape-eval run after /shape-plan writes the eval in the plan's evals folder, and no build play's inputs name that folder."}}}, {"asked": "what keeps builders out until encryption", "found": "only a read rule, until eval encryption (#828)", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 21, "end": 21, "fingerprint": "sha256:27a7e14191e2f408c7e860900377e12b7515cfc8d553f086f94c224e0d9e04f9", "text": "- Until eval encryption (#828) exists, only a read rule keeps builders out of the evals folder.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 18, "end": 24, "text": "- The eval checks from the outside, on the slice's surface. For Garura that surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project.\n- The running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (`guides/<slug>.md`).\n- When the eval cannot test a goal, an expectation or a failure condition yet, it says so.\n- Until eval encryption (#828) exists, only a read rule keeps builders out of the evals folder.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given a plan with an epic and its stories, when the product owner runs /shape-eval, then the eval is in the plan's evals folder."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261025-006", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which surface does the tester use?", "answer": "the Claude Code command line, where the product owner runs the three plays", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:40:44Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the surface of the kept slice", "found": "the slice record names the Claude Code command line, where the product owner runs the three plays", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 15, "end": 20, "fingerprint": "sha256:4a2bf683f15724c3a5fd145970358fdd638197e1df4e8c2c04441040277a4130", "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent", "version": null, "around": {"start": 12, "end": 20, "text": "  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\nsurface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}, {"asked": "where /shape-slice is run", "found": "the product owner runs /shape-slice 788 in Claude Code", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-slice/fn-795/feature.md", "start": 46, "end": 47, "fingerprint": "sha256:4f934f7801765d5474d9c5f302c623ba154044728c6724ff60ba8a7e12e38b9d", "text": "- Context: serves the product owner, who runs it in Claude Code; built in #795 (core/components/plays/shape-slice/): it reads the intent from the model and writes the intent page from the issue when the model has none, asks within the tier, reuses a slice that serves, fills the model, writes the slice and its record, and stops at a typed yes / change / stop.\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-slice 788 in Claude Code and finds one slice in the spine, the hidden file in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no other new file outside the model.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 43, "end": 47, "text": "- Fails if: /shape-slice writes a plan, an epic, a story or an eval.\n- Fails if: a new slice is made for an intent that a slice already serves.\n- Fails if: the hidden file is not written, or a failure condition in it has no recovery or more than one.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who runs it in Claude Code; built in #795 (core/components/plays/shape-slice/): it reads the intent from the model and writes the intent page from the issue when the model has none, asks within the tier, reuses a slice that serves, fills the model, writes the slice and its record, and stops at a typed yes / change / stop.\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-slice 788 in Claude Code and finds one slice in the spine, the hidden file in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no other new file outside the model."}}}, {"asked": "where /shape-plan is run", "found": "the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 48, "end": 48, "fingerprint": "sha256:2e7f16d37787301d207efb8b857691df53d45a1dcfe971b4c89b56e372fb2473", "text": "- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code after /shape-slice and finds the plan file, one epic and one story for each feature, with no failure line in any story.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 45, "end": 48, "text": "- Fails if: a story or the plan file holds a failure condition or a recovery condition.\n- Fails if: a second run makes a second epic for the slice or a second story for one feature.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who runs and tracks the plan, and the build play, which reads the stories; reads the slice from the spine and the ICE of each feature and its capability; writes .garura/project/plans/ and the tracker; out are the slice, the hidden file, the eval and the build. Not built yet (#818).\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code after /shape-slice and finds the plan file, one epic and one story for each feature, with no failure line in any story."}}}, {"asked": "where /shape-eval is run", "found": "the product owner runs /shape-eval 788 in Claude Code", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 43, "end": 43, "fingerprint": "sha256:599dc67c40815b9c5b09669ff0bf77a77bb80008d40011814d83473a68116505", "text": "- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-eval 788 in Claude Code after /shape-plan and finds the eval in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no build play's inputs name that folder.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 40, "end": 43, "text": "- Fails if: a story's goal or expectation, or a failure condition in the hidden file, has no check, and the eval does not say that it cannot test it yet.\n- Fails if: a handoff plan that the eval writes names a failure condition, its id or the check.\n- Context: serves the product owner; for Garura the surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project; the running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (guides/<slug>.md). Not built yet (#798).\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-eval 788 in Claude Code after /shape-plan and finds the eval in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no build play's inputs name that folder."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261025-007", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Who tests the slice there?", "answer": "the product owner, who names the work and confirms each part", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:40:45Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who asks for the intent and confirms each part", "found": "the product owner names the work and confirms each part; asked by the product owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 3, "end": 7, "fingerprint": "sha256:0755579b4d038a46af0e134c15ce2d131aa6f3c9cd3a21d090b2732e1c0d7d3d", "text": "**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 10, "text": "# Agents design a named piece of work\n\n**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design."}}}, {"asked": "whom the domain serves", "found": "the product owner, who names the work and approves its design", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/domain.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:60fa1114342177f7ae0d127a29930b41b3f1d37de6b40b025f628714c9d9a876", "text": "This domain turns a business intent into work that agents can build and that a check from the outside can prove. It serves the product owner, who names the work and approves its design, and the plays that build from that design. Its job comes before the build: it shapes one slice that a person can test end to end, it plans that slice as work items in the tracker, and it writes the eval that says if the intent is met. It does not build, check or release the work, and it never lets a builder read the eval.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Theme: Software delivery planning\n\n## Intent\nThis domain turns a business intent into work that agents can build and that a check from the outside can prove. It serves the product owner, who names the work and approves its design, and the plays that build from that design. Its job comes before the build: it shapes one slice that a person can test end to end, it plans that slice as work items in the tracker, and it writes the eval that says if the intent is met. It does not build, check or release the work, and it never lets a builder read the eval.\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "the tester of the kept slice", "found": "persona_ref product-owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 18, "end": 18, "fingerprint": "sha256:3d969030c31daee3dcfff40b9e7df245f6f7fbbfa1285f1acf0886cf77238ddf", "text": "  persona_ref: product-owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 15, "end": 20, "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261025-008", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which features does the slice need?", "answer": "fn-795 (/shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file), fn-818 (/shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories) and fn-798 (/shape-eval writes the hidden eval)", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:40:45Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what the proof asks the design to have", "found": "a slice, a plan with one epic and one story per feature, and an eval from the outside", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 9, "end": 16, "fingerprint": "sha256:56d22d892ded828350453c4c92205dc8717a4e6f4c18201dbaa21c45186a05e4", "text": "**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design.\n- The design has a slice that one person can test end to end on one surface, with the features it needs in build order.\n- The design has a plan that a person can run and track: the plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature.\n- The design has an eval that tests, from the outside, if the business intent is met.\n- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.\n- A play runs each step. No step is done by hand.\n- The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 6, "end": 19, "text": "\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design.\n- The design has a slice that one person can test end to end on one surface, with the features it needs in build order.\n- The design has a plan that a person can run and track: the plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature.\n- The design has an eval that tests, from the outside, if the business intent is met.\n- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.\n- A play runs each step. No step is done by hand.\n- The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.\n\n**Must not:** Do not send the slice, the plan or the eval to the tracker before the product owner confirms it, and do not start a build before that. Do not let a builder read the eval. Do not shape an ICE that is not ready. Do not ask the person a question that the model or memory answers. Do not include the design, build, test or validation of an epic (#819), the release plays or /learn-outcomes, or the upgrade of an older product model (#835).\n"}}}, {"asked": "which feature writes the slice", "found": "fn-795: /shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-slice/fn-795/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:e2ee291f90ccf3c89354da90015cf1f7868c5b1391201868ed80a3eac9446eb7", "text": "/shape-slice <intent> reads the business intent and the product model, asks the person only what the model and memory do not answer, and writes one slice into the spine with its link to the intent. It also writes the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md, one entry for each feature) in the plan's evals folder, and a thin ICE for each part the slice needs that has no ICE (ontology v11, ADR 052). It writes no plan, no epic, no story and no eval. Built in #795. Not built yet: the hidden file and the thin ICE need the play's /edit-play change (#842).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file\n\n## What it does\n/shape-slice <intent> reads the business intent and the product model, asks the person only what the model and memory do not answer, and writes one slice into the spine with its link to the intent. It also writes the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md, one entry for each feature) in the plan's evals folder, and a thin ICE for each part the slice needs that has no ICE (ontology v11, ADR 052). It writes no plan, no epic, no story and no eval. Built in #795. Not built yet: the hidden file and the thin ICE need the play's /edit-play change (#842).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "which feature writes the plan", "found": "fn-818: /shape-plan writes the plan file, one epic and one story per feature", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:994885950cc86d2453e28af308067e90cd83ed82d1ef9626e2a157812c7b8819", "text": "/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories\n\n## What it does\n/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "which feature writes the eval", "found": "fn-798: /shape-eval writes the eval in the plan's evals folder", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:ae8291267fc5bc60fcf93f3c53ca8d86fc4b4def2337ec155e3bc7eccf5bee90", "text": "/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No builder reads that folder. Not built yet (#798).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-eval writes the hidden eval\n\n## What it does\n/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No builder reads that folder. Not built yet (#798).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261025-009", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In what order are the features built?", "answer": "fn-795, then fn-818, then fn-798", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:40:45Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the order of the shaping plays", "found": "three plays in a row: shape the slice, build the plan, build the eval (ADR 049)", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/domain.md", "start": 13, "end": 13, "fingerprint": "sha256:5daa5ffd2e245c855bab56e3b601e8f2b76fceaee1054e40ea35ec34e2643eb3", "text": "- docs/adr/049-a-slice-is-shaped-then-planned-then-given-its-eval.md, Decision 1: 'the shaping work is three plays in a row: shape the slice, build the plan, build the eval.'", "version": null, "around": {"start": 10, "end": 16, "text": "- User Story Mapping: Discover the Whole Story, Build the Right Product (O'Reilly, 2014, ISBN 9781491904909, https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/user-story-mapping/9781491904893/): it has a chapter on planning to build less, which slices out a minimum release that a person can use and test end to end.\n- Specification by Example: How Successful Teams Deliver the Right Software (Manning, 2011, https://oreilly.com/library/view/specification-by-example/9781617290084): realistic examples are the development target, the acceptance criteria and the tests, agreed before the build and checked from the outside.\n- Epics, stories, and initiatives (Atlassian, https://www.atlassian.com/agile/project-management/epics-stories-themes): an epic holds several stories, and initiatives sit above epics.\n- docs/adr/049-a-slice-is-shaped-then-planned-then-given-its-eval.md, Decision 1: 'the shaping work is three plays in a row: shape the slice, build the plan, build the eval.'\n- docs/philosophy/idsd.md, IDSD in One Page: the Shape loop, 'the product is ready to build in slices'; and 'The Plan Is the Human's Interface'.\n- docs/philosophy/garura-reference-implementation.md, The Builder/Validator Barrier: the evals are kept away from the builders.\n- Memory (phoenix) knowledge/domains/*.md, the ten shelves: no shelf has a trigger for software delivery work (placement-routing.json, unmatched)."}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-plan needs first", "found": "it runs after /shape-slice and needs the slice to exist", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 17, "end": 17, "fingerprint": "sha256:cd1a3ef4d2fcab7ab93c47753768264fb32361bdd96127b65219ca5e239e4a7e", "text": "- The play runs after /shape-slice, on its own, and needs the slice to exist.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 14, "end": 20, "text": "- Thin: the fields of the plan file and of each story are not set yet.\n\n## Rules & behavior\n- The play runs after /shape-slice, on its own, and needs the slice to exist.\n- Each story carries the goal, the limits, the expectations and the Context guidance from its feature's ICE and its capability's ICE.\n- The play never writes a failure or recovery condition. The slice's hidden file belongs to /shape-slice (decision 6).\n- A second run finds the plan, the epic and the stories that exist, and makes no copies."}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-eval needs first", "found": "it runs after /shape-plan and reads only the epic, its stories and the hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 16, "end": 17, "fingerprint": "sha256:57ee99456b2b4c248d109266b094a8b27bb9a99b5b76b16a9dc2bd75b362d9ae", "text": "- The play runs after /shape-plan, on its own.\n- It reads only the epic, its stories and the hidden file. It never reads an ICE page, the usage guide or the code.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 13, "end": 20, "text": "- Thin: the format of the eval and of the handoff plan is not set yet.\n\n## Rules & behavior\n- The play runs after /shape-plan, on its own.\n- It reads only the epic, its stories and the hidden file. It never reads an ICE page, the usage guide or the code.\n- The eval checks from the outside, on the slice's surface. For Garura that surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project.\n- The running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (`guides/<slug>.md`).\n- When the eval cannot test a goal, an expectation or a failure condition yet, it says so."}}}], "from_update": null}
