+      "topic": "change",
+      "blocking": false,
+      "question": "When a feature is added to a slice or taken out of it after its plan exists, what must the plan play do with the stories of that slice?",
+      "why": "If the plan play makes new stories, or deletes old ones, without a rule, the plan and the tracker stop agreeing, or the work already done on a story is lost.",
+      "examples": [
+        "a shop: an order changes after packing, so the new item goes in the same parcel and the removed item goes back to the shelf, with a note on the order",
+        "a clinic: a treatment plan drops one visit, so that visit is cancelled but kept in the record, and a new visit is booked",
+        "a building project: one room is added to the plan, so a new task is added under the same project, and no task is deleted"
+      ],
+      "assume": "The plan play adds one story for each feature that comes in, closes the story of each feature that goes out with a note, deletes nothing, and changes nothing in the tracker before the product owner's yes.",
+      "settled": false,
+      "basis": {
+        "kind": "model",
+        "ref": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md:20-22 (a second run makes no copies; nothing goes to the tracker before the yes; what the play does when the slice changes is not set yet) and :44-46 (fails if a feature of the slice has no story, or a second story is made for one feature)"
+      },
+      "proposed_answer": "When a feature comes into the slice, the plan play adds one story for it, so that each feature of the slice has a story; it makes no second story for a feature that has one; and nothing goes to the tracker before the product owner's yes. What it does with the story of a feature that goes out is not set by the model: the product owner says."
+    },
