s/shape-slice/): it reads the intent from the model and writes the intent page from the issue when the model has none, asks within the tier, reuses a slice that serves, fills the model, writes the slice and its record, and stops at a typed yes / change / stop.\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-slice 788 in Claude Code and finds one slice in the spine, the hidden file in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no other new file outside the model.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 43, "end": 47, "text": "- Fails if: /shape-slice writes a plan, an epic, a story or an eval.\n- Fails if: a new slice is made for an intent that a slice already serves.\n- Fails if: the hidden file is not written, or a failure condition in it has no recovery or more than one.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who runs it in Claude Code; built in #795 (core/components/plays/shape-slice/): it reads the intent from the model and writes the intent page from the issue when the model has none, asks within the tier, reuses a slice that serves, fills the model, writes the slice and its record, and stops at a typed yes / change / stop.\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-slice 788 in Claude Code and finds one slice in the spine, the hidden file in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no other new file outside the model."}}}, {"asked": "where /shape-plan is run", "found": "the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 48, "end": 48, "fingerprint": "sha256:2e7f16d37787301d207efb8b857691df53d45a1dcfe971b4c89b56e372fb2473", "text": "- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code after /shape-slice and finds the plan file, one epic and one story for each feature, with no failure line in any story.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 45, "end": 48, "text": "- Fails if: a story or the plan file holds a failure condition or a recovery condition.\n- Fails if: a second run makes a second epic for the slice or a second story for one feature.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who runs and tracks the plan, and the build play, which reads the stories; reads the slice from the spine and the ICE of each feature and its capability; writes .garura/project/plans/ and the tracker; out are the slice, the hidden file, the eval and the build. Not built yet (#818).\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code after /shape-slice and finds the plan file, one epic and one story for each feature, with no failure line in any story."}}}, {"asked": "where /shape-eval is run", "found": "the product owner runs /shape-eval 788 in Claude Code", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 43, "end": 43, "fingerprint": "sha256:599dc67c40815b9c5b09669ff0bf77a77bb80008d40011814d83473a68116505", "text": "- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-eval 788 in Claude Code after /shape-plan and finds the eval in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no build play's inputs name that folder.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 40, "end": 43, "text": "- Fails if: a story's goal or expectation, or a failure condition in the hidden file, has no check, and the eval does not say that it cannot test it yet.\n- Fails if: a handoff plan that the eval writes names a failure condition, its id or the check.\n- Context: serves the product owner; for Garura the surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project; the running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (guides/<slug>.md). Not built yet (#798).\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-eval 788 in Claude Code after /shape-plan and finds the eval in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no build play's inputs name that folder."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-007", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Who tests the slice there?", "answer": "the product owner, who names the work and confirms each part", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:40:45Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who asks for the intent and confirms each part", "found": "the product owner names the work and confirms each part; asked by the product owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 3, "end": 7, "fingerprint": "sha256:0755579b4d038a46af0e134c15ce2d131aa6f3c9cd3a21d090b2732e1c0d7d3d", "text": "**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 10, "text": "# Agents design a named piece of work\n\n**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design."}}}, {"asked": "whom the domain serves", "found": "the product owner, who names the work and approves its design", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/domain.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:60fa1114342177f7ae0d127a29930b41b3f1d37de6b40b025f628714c9d9a876", "text": "This domain turns a business intent into work that agents can build and that a check from the outside can prove. It serves the product owner, who names the work and approves its design, and the plays that build from that design. Its job comes before the build: it shapes one slice that a person can test end to end, it plans that slice as work items in the tracker, and it writes the eval that says if the intent is met. It does not build, check or release the work, and it never lets a builder read the eval.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Theme: Software delivery planning\n\n## Intent\nThis domain turns a business intent into work that agents can build and that a check from the outside can prove. It serves the product owner, who names the work and approves its design, and the plays that build from that design. Its job comes before the build: it shapes one slice that a person can test end to end, it plans that slice as work items in the tracker, and it writes the eval that says if the intent is met. It does not build, check or release the work, and it never lets a builder read the eval.\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "the tester of the kept slice", "found": "persona_ref product-owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 18, "end": 18, "fingerprint": "sha256:3d969030c31daee3dcfff40b9e7df245f6f7fbbfa1285f1acf0886cf77238ddf", "text": "  persona_ref: product-owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 15, "end": 20, "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-008", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which features does the slice need?", "answer": "fn-795 (/shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file), fn-818 (/shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories) and fn-798 (/shape-eval writes the hidden eval)", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:40:45Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what the proof asks the design to have", "found": "a slice, a plan with one epic and one story per feature, and an eval from the outside", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 9, "end": 16, "fingerprint": "sha256:56d22d892ded828350453c4c92205dc8717a4e6f4c18201dbaa21c45186a05e4", "text": "**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design.\n- The design has a slice that one person can test end to end on one surface, with the features it needs in build order.\n- The design has a plan that a person can run and track: the plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature.\n- The design has an eval that tests, from the outside, if the business intent is met.\n- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.\n- A play runs each step. No step is done by hand.\n- The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 6, "end": 19, "text": "\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design.\n- The design has a slice that one person can test end to end on one surface, with the features it needs in build order.\n- The design has a plan that a person can run and track: the plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature.\n- The design has an eval that tests, from the outside, if the business intent is met.\n- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.\n- A play runs each step. No step is done by hand.\n- The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.\n\n**Must not:** Do not send the slice, the plan or the eval to the tracker before the product owner confirms it, and do not start a build before that. Do not let a builder read the eval. Do not shape an ICE that is not ready. Do not ask the person a question that the model or memory answers. Do not include the design, build, test or validation of an epic (#819), the release plays or /learn-outcomes, or the upgrade of an older product model (#835).\n"}}}, {"asked": "which feature writes the slice", "found": "fn-795: /shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-slice/fn-795/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:e2ee291f90ccf3c89354da90015cf1f7868c5b1391201868ed80a3eac9446eb7", "text": "/shape-slice <intent> reads the business intent and the product model, asks the person only what the model and memory do not answer, and writes one slice into the spine with its link to the intent. It also writes the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md, one entry for each feature) in the plan's evals folder, and a thin ICE for each part the slice needs that has no ICE (ontology v11, ADR 052). It writes no plan, no epic, no story and no eval. Built in #795. Not built yet: the hidden file and the thin ICE need the play's /edit-play change (#842).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file\n\n## What it does\n/shape-slice <intent> reads the business intent and the product model, asks the person only what the model and memory do not answer, and writes one slice into the spine with its link to the intent. It also writes the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md, one entry for each feature) in the plan's evals folder, and a thin ICE for each part the slice needs that has no ICE (ontology v11, ADR 052). It writes no plan, no epic, no story and no eval. Built in #795. Not built yet: the hidden file and the thin ICE need the play's /edit-play change (#842).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "which feature writes the plan", "found": "fn-818: /shape-plan writes the plan file, one epic and one story per feature", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:994885950cc86d2453e28af308067e90cd83ed82d1ef9626e2a157812c7b8819", "text": "/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories\n\n## What it does\n/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "which feature writes the eval", "found": "fn-798: /shape-eval writes the eval in the plan's evals folder", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:ae8291267fc5bc60fcf93f3c53ca8d86fc4b4def2337ec155e3bc7eccf5bee90", "text": "/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No builder reads that folder. Not built yet (#798).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-eval writes the hidden eval\n\n## What it does\n/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No builder reads that folder. Not built yet (#798).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-009", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In what order are the features built?", "answer": "fn-795, then fn-818, then fn-798", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:40:45Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the order of the shaping plays", "found": "three plays in a row: shape the slice, build the plan, build the eval (ADR 049)", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/domain.md", "start": 13, "end": 13, "fingerprint": "sha256:5daa5ffd2e245c855bab56e3b601e8f2b76fceaee1054e40ea35ec34e2643eb3", "text": "- docs/adr/049-a-slice-is-shaped-then-planned-then-given-its-eval.md, Decision 1: 'the shaping work is three plays in a row: shape the slice, build the plan, build the eval.'", "version": null, "around": {"start": 10, "end": 16, "text": "- User Story Mapping: Discover the Whole Story, Build the Right Product (O'Reilly, 2014, ISBN 9781491904909, https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/user-story-mapping/9781491904893/): it has a chapter on planning to build less, which slices out a minimum release that a person can use and test end to end.\n- Specification by Example: How Successful Teams Deliver the Right Software (Manning, 2011, https://oreilly.com/library/view/specification-by-example/9781617290084): realistic examples are the development target, the acceptance criteria and the tests, agreed before the build and checked from the outside.\n- Epics, stories, and initiatives (Atlassian, https://www.atlassian.com/agile/project-management/epics-stories-themes): an epic holds several stories, and initiatives sit above epics.\n- docs/adr/049-a-slice-is-shaped-then-planned-then-given-its-eval.md, Decision 1: 'the shaping work is three plays in a row: shape the slice, build the plan, build the eval.'\n- docs/philosophy/idsd.md, IDSD in One Page: the Shape loop, 'the product is ready to build in slices'; and 'The Plan Is the Human's Interface'.\n- docs/philosophy/garura-reference-implementation.md, The Builder/Validator Barrier: the evals are kept away from the builders.\n- Memory (phoenix) knowledge/domains/*.md, the ten shelves: no shelf has a trigger for software delivery work (placement-routing.json, unmatched)."}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-plan needs first", "found": "it runs after /shape-slice and needs the slice to exist", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 17, "end": 17, "fingerprint": "sha256:cd1a3ef4d2fcab7ab93c47753768264fb32361bdd96127b65219ca5e239e4a7e", "text": "- The play runs after /shape-slice, on its own, and needs the slice to exist.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 14, "end": 20, "text": "- Thin: the fields of the plan file and of each story are not set yet.\n\n## Rules & behavior\n- The play runs after /shape-slice, on its own, and needs the slice to exist.\n- Each story carries the goal, the limits, the expectations and the Context guidance from its feature's ICE and its capability's ICE.\n- The play never writes a failure or recovery condition. The slice's hidden file belongs to /shape-slice (decision 6).\n- A second run finds the plan, the epic and the stories that exist, and makes no copies."}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-eval needs first", "found": "it runs after /shape-plan and reads only the epic, its stories and the hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 16, "end": 17, "fingerprint": "sha256:57ee99456b2b4c248d109266b094a8b27bb9a99b5b76b16a9dc2bd75b362d9ae", "text": "- The play runs after /shape-plan, on its own.\n- It reads only the epic, its stories and the hidden file. It never reads an ICE page, the usage guide or the code.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 13, "end": 20, "text": "- Thin: the format of the eval and of the handoff plan is not set yet.\n\n## Rules & behavior\n- The play runs after /shape-plan, on its own.\n- It reads only the epic, its stories and the hidden file. It never reads an ICE page, the usage guide or the code.\n- The eval checks from the outside, on the slice's surface. For Garura that surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project.\n- The running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (`guides/<slug>.md`).\n- When the eval cannot test a goal, an expectation or a failure condition yet, it says so."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-010", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which slice serves business intent bi-788, and does it change?", "answer": "sl-intent-to-design serves bi-788 and stays as it is: pull_in is empty and push_out is empty, because the kept slice already holds fn-795, fn-818 and fn-798, the same features in the same order as the shaped slice, and each still serves bi-788.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:42:14Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the rule that matched a kept slice to the intent", "found": "slice sl-intent-to-design already lists business intent bi-788", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "866/context/shape-slice/serving.json", "start": 3, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:b09c15604a608807eda5bac746b47ed1020d856921e45c8b36daed6d365ab6e5", "text": "  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "{\n  \"match\": \"sl-intent-to-design\",\n  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",\n  \"reuse_args\": [\n    \"--reuse\",\n    \"sl-intent-to-design\""}}}, {"asked": "the kept slice's features and intents in the spine", "found": "sl-intent-to-design holds fn-795, fn-818, fn-798 and serves bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 464, "end": 473, "fingerprint": "sha256:0ea3c68ccb38675e601173f5a27bf2f81f11ad39bf2d12122448c9d9d119e308", "text": "- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "version": null, "around": {"start": 461, "end": 473, "text": "      gate: ready-check and linter tests; spine before/after diff on the rename\n  compliance: []\nslices:\n- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml"}}}, {"asked": "whether fn-795 still serves the intent", "found": "fn-795 serves bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 414, "end": 418, "fingerprint": "sha256:792230356c117a8bf5b9905dde822d81c0b841342d022c04e0aec6a182ec0933", "text": "- id: fn-795\n  slug: fn-795\n  capability: cap-shape-slice\n  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 411, "end": 421, "text": "  - fn-741\n  identified_by: ''\n  issue: 748\n- id: fn-795\n  slug: fn-795\n  capability: cap-shape-slice\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From a business intent, /shape-slice writes one slice, its link to the\n    intent and its hidden file, and no plan, epic, story or eval."}}}, {"asked": "whether fn-818 still serves the intent", "found": "fn-818 serves bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 427, "end": 431, "fingerprint": "sha256:68143928ae9a889ca6788aabf83c18ed22ecab904af47d16036b80ec834aedd2", "text": "- id: fn-818\n  slug: fn-818\n  capability: cap-718\n  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 424, "end": 434, "text": "    created_by: /shape-slice\n    deepen: true\n    thin: true\n- id: fn-818\n  slug: fn-818\n  capability: cap-718\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From a shaped slice, /shape-plan writes the intent's one plan file, one\n    epic for the slice and one story for each feature."}}}, {"asked": "whether fn-798 still serves the intent", "found": "fn-798 serves bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 440, "end": 444, "fingerprint": "sha256:ef5dcce9289e1b7a1ac5cfa3209f5155717e41c4c63c7ff7898c19ece3fc56db", "text": "- id: fn-798\n  slug: fn-798\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 437, "end": 447, "text": "    created_by: /shape-slice\n    deepen: true\n    thin: true\n- id: fn-798\n  slug: fn-798\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From the plan's epic and stories, /shape-eval writes the eval for the\n    business intent in the plan's evals folder, where no builder reads."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-011", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which surface does the tester use?", "answer": "the Claude Code command line, where the product owner runs the three plays", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:47:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the surface of the kept slice", "found": "the slice record names the Claude Code command line, where the product owner runs the three plays", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 15, "end": 20, "fingerprint": "sha256:4a2bf683f15724c3a5fd145970358fdd638197e1df4e8c2c04441040277a4130", "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent", "version": null, "around": {"start": 12, "end": 20, "text": "  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\nsurface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}, {"asked": "where /shape-slice is run", "found": "the product owner runs /shape-slice 788 in Claude Code", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-slice/fn-795/feature.md", "start": 46, "end": 47, "fingerprint": "sha256:4f934f7801765d5474d9c5f302c623ba154044728c6724ff60ba8a7e12e38b9d", "text": "- Context: serves the product owner, who runs it in Claude Code; built in #795 (core/components/plays/shape-slice/): it reads the intent from the model and writes the intent page from the issue when the model has none, asks within the tier, reuses a slice that serves, fills the model, writes the slice and its record, and stops at a typed yes / change / stop.\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-slice 788 in Claude Code and finds one slice in the spine, the hidden file in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no other new file outside the model.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 43, "end": 47, "text": "- Fails if: /shape-slice writes a plan, an epic, a story or an eval.\n- Fails if: a new slice is made for an intent that a slice already serves.\n- Fails if: the hidden file is not written, or a failure condition in it has no recovery or more than one.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who runs it in Claude Code; built in #795 (core/components/plays/shape-slice/): it reads the intent from the model and writes the intent page from the issue when the model has none, asks within the tier, reuses a slice that serves, fills the model, writes the slice and its record, and stops at a typed yes / change / stop.\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-slice 788 in Claude Code and finds one slice in the spine, the hidden file in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no other new file outside the model."}}}, {"asked": "where /shape-plan is run", "found": "the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 48, "end": 48, "fingerprint": "sha256:2e7f16d37787301d207efb8b857691df53d45a1dcfe971b4c89b56e372fb2473", "text": "- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code after /shape-slice and finds the plan file, one epic and one story for each feature, with no failure line in any story.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 45, "end": 48, "text": "- Fails if: a story or the plan file holds a failure condition or a recovery condition.\n- Fails if: a second run makes a second epic for the slice or a second story for one feature.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who runs and tracks the plan, and the build play, which reads the stories; reads the slice from the spine and the ICE of each feature and its capability; writes .garura/project/plans/ and the tracker; out are the slice, the hidden file, the eval and the build. Not built yet (#818).\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code after /shape-slice and finds the plan file, one epic and one story for each feature, with no failure line in any story."}}}, {"asked": "where /shape-eval is run", "found": "the product owner runs /shape-eval 788 in Claude Code", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 43, "end": 43, "fingerprint": "sha256:599dc67c40815b9c5b09669ff0bf77a77bb80008d40011814d83473a68116505", "text": "- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-eval 788 in Claude Code after /shape-plan and finds the eval in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no build play's inputs name that folder.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 40, "end": 43, "text": "- Fails if: a story's goal or expectation, or a failure condition in the hidden file, has no check, and the eval does not say that it cannot test it yet.\n- Fails if: a handoff plan that the eval writes names a failure condition, its id or the check.\n- Context: serves the product owner; for Garura the surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project; the running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (guides/<slug>.md). Not built yet (#798).\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-eval 788 in Claude Code after /shape-plan and finds the eval in plans/788/evals/<slug>/, and no build play's inputs name that folder."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-012", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Who tests the slice there?", "answer": "the product owner, who names the work and confirms each part", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:47:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who asks for the intent and confirms each part", "found": "the product owner names the work and confirms each part; asked by the product owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 3, "end": 7, "fingerprint": "sha256:0755579b4d038a46af0e134c15ce2d131aa6f3c9cd3a21d090b2732e1c0d7d3d", "text": "**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 10, "text": "# Agents design a named piece of work\n\n**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design."}}}, {"asked": "whom the domain serves", "found": "the product owner, who names the work and approves its design", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/domain.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:60fa1114342177f7ae0d127a29930b41b3f1d37de6b40b025f628714c9d9a876", "text": "This domain turns a business intent into work that agents can build and that a check from the outside can prove. It serves the product owner, who names the work and approves its design, and the plays that build from that design. Its job comes before the build: it shapes one slice that a person can test end to end, it plans that slice as work items in the tracker, and it writes the eval that says if the intent is met. It does not build, check or release the work, and it never lets a builder read the eval.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Theme: Software delivery planning\n\n## Intent\nThis domain turns a business intent into work that agents can build and that a check from the outside can prove. It serves the product owner, who names the work and approves its design, and the plays that build from that design. Its job comes before the build: it shapes one slice that a person can test end to end, it plans that slice as work items in the tracker, and it writes the eval that says if the intent is met. It does not build, check or release the work, and it never lets a builder read the eval.\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "the tester of the kept slice", "found": "persona_ref product-owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 18, "end": 18, "fingerprint": "sha256:3d969030c31daee3dcfff40b9e7df245f6f7fbbfa1285f1acf0886cf77238ddf", "text": "  persona_ref: product-owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 15, "end": 20, "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-013", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which features does the slice need?", "answer": "fn-795 (/shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file), fn-818 (/shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories) and fn-798 (/shape-eval writes the hidden eval)", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:47:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what the proof asks the design to have", "found": "a slice, a plan with one epic and one story per feature, and an eval from the outside", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 9, "end": 16, "fingerprint": "sha256:56d22d892ded828350453c4c92205dc8717a4e6f4c18201dbaa21c45186a05e4", "text": "**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design.\n- The design has a slice that one person can test end to end on one surface, with the features it needs in build order.\n- The design has a plan that a person can run and track: the plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature.\n- The design has an eval that tests, from the outside, if the business intent is met.\n- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.\n- A play runs each step. No step is done by hand.\n- The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 6, "end": 19, "text": "\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design.\n- The design has a slice that one person can test end to end on one surface, with the features it needs in build order.\n- The design has a plan that a person can run and track: the plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature.\n- The design has an eval that tests, from the outside, if the business intent is met.\n- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.\n- A play runs each step. No step is done by hand.\n- The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.\n\n**Must not:** Do not send the slice, the plan or the eval to the tracker before the product owner confirms it, and do not start a build before that. Do not let a builder read the eval. Do not shape an ICE that is not ready. Do not ask the person a question that the model or memory answers. Do not include the design, build, test or validation of an epic (#819), the release plays or /learn-outcomes, or the upgrade of an older product model (#835).\n"}}}, {"asked": "which feature writes the slice", "found": "fn-795: /shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-slice/fn-795/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:e2ee291f90ccf3c89354da90015cf1f7868c5b1391201868ed80a3eac9446eb7", "text": "/shape-slice <intent> reads the business intent and the product model, asks the person only what the model and memory do not answer, and writes one slice into the spine with its link to the intent. It also writes the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md, one entry for each feature) in the plan's evals folder, and a thin ICE for each part the slice needs that has no ICE (ontology v11, ADR 052). It writes no plan, no epic, no story and no eval. Built in #795. Not built yet: the hidden file and the thin ICE need the play's /edit-play change (#842).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file\n\n## What it does\n/shape-slice <intent> reads the business intent and the product model, asks the person only what the model and memory do not answer, and writes one slice into the spine with its link to the intent. It also writes the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md, one entry for each feature) in the plan's evals folder, and a thin ICE for each part the slice needs that has no ICE (ontology v11, ADR 052). It writes no plan, no epic, no story and no eval. Built in #795. Not built yet: the hidden file and the thin ICE need the play's /edit-play change (#842).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "which feature writes the plan", "found": "fn-818: /shape-plan writes the plan file, one epic and one story per feature", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:994885950cc86d2453e28af308067e90cd83ed82d1ef9626e2a157812c7b8819", "text": "/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories\n\n## What it does\n/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "which feature writes the eval", "found": "fn-798: /shape-eval writes the eval in the plan's evals folder", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:ae8291267fc5bc60fcf93f3c53ca8d86fc4b4def2337ec155e3bc7eccf5bee90", "text": "/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No builder reads that folder. Not built yet (#798).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-eval writes the hidden eval\n\n## What it does\n/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No builder reads that folder. Not built yet (#798).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-014", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In what order are the features built?", "answer": "fn-795, then fn-818, then fn-798", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:47:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the order of the shaping plays", "found": "three plays in a row: shape the slice, build the plan, build the eval (ADR 049)", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/domain.md", "start": 13, "end": 13, "fingerprint": "sha256:5daa5ffd2e245c855bab56e3b601e8f2b76fceaee1054e40ea35ec34e2643eb3", "text": "- docs/adr/049-a-slice-is-shaped-then-planned-then-given-its-eval.md, Decision 1: 'the shaping work is three plays in a row: shape the slice, build the plan, build the eval.'", "version": null, "around": {"start": 10, "end": 16, "text": "- User Story Mapping: Discover the Whole Story, Build the Right Product (O'Reilly, 2014, ISBN 9781491904909, https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/user-story-mapping/9781491904893/): it has a chapter on planning to build less, which slices out a minimum release that a person can use and test end to end.\n- Specification by Example: How Successful Teams Deliver the Right Software (Manning, 2011, https://oreilly.com/library/view/specification-by-example/9781617290084): realistic examples are the development target, the acceptance criteria and the tests, agreed before the build and checked from the outside.\n- Epics, stories, and initiatives (Atlassian, https://www.atlassian.com/agile/project-management/epics-stories-themes): an epic holds several stories, and initiatives sit above epics.\n- docs/adr/049-a-slice-is-shaped-then-planned-then-given-its-eval.md, Decision 1: 'the shaping work is three plays in a row: shape the slice, build the plan, build the eval.'\n- docs/philosophy/idsd.md, IDSD in One Page: the Shape loop, 'the product is ready to build in slices'; and 'The Plan Is the Human's Interface'.\n- docs/philosophy/garura-reference-implementation.md, The Builder/Validator Barrier: the evals are kept away from the builders.\n- Memory (phoenix) knowledge/domains/*.md, the ten shelves: no shelf has a trigger for software delivery work (placement-routing.json, unmatched)."}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-plan needs first", "found": "it runs after /shape-slice and needs the slice to exist", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 17, "end": 17, "fingerprint": "sha256:cd1a3ef4d2fcab7ab93c47753768264fb32361bdd96127b65219ca5e239e4a7e", "text": "- The play runs after /shape-slice, on its own, and needs the slice to exist.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 14, "end": 20, "text": "- Thin: the fields of the plan file and of each story are not set yet.\n\n## Rules & behavior\n- The play runs after /shape-slice, on its own, and needs the slice to exist.\n- Each story carries the goal, the limits, the expectations and the Context guidance from its feature's ICE and its capability's ICE.\n- The play never writes a failure or recovery condition. The slice's hidden file belongs to /shape-slice (decision 6).\n- A second run finds the plan, the epic and the stories that exist, and makes no copies."}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-eval needs first", "found": "it runs after /shape-plan and reads only the epic, its stories and the hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start