c19ece3fc56db", "text": "- id: fn-798\n  slug: fn-798\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 437, "end": 447, "text": "    created_by: /shape-slice\n    deepen: true\n    thin: true\n- id: fn-798\n  slug: fn-798\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From the plan's epic and stories, /shape-eval writes the eval for the\n    business intent in the plan's evals folder, where no builder reads."}}}, {"asked": "the kept slice's record", "found": "sl-intent-to-design holds fn-795, fn-818, fn-798 on the Claude Code command line and serves bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 1, "end": 20, "fingerprint": "sha256:f4313a8f1e0f497b4d6d6534c7a8a960aeadf92809db99cf9b9b076f07e9e7c8", "text": "slice:\n  id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  name: From a named piece of work to its design\n  outcome: The product owner runs three plays on a business intent and gets a slice\n    to test, a plan with one epic and one story for each feature, and an eval that\n    no builder can read.\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\nsurface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 20, "text": "slice:\n  id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  name: From a named piece of work to its design\n  outcome: The product owner runs three plays on a business intent and gets a slice\n    to test, a plan with one epic and one story for each feature, and an eval that\n    no builder can read.\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\nsurface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-016", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "When a feature is added to a slice or taken out of it after its plan exists, what must the plan play do with the stories of that slice?", "answer": "When a feature comes into the slice, the plan play adds one story for it, so that each feature of the slice has a story; it makes no second story for a feature that has one; and nothing goes to the tracker before the product owner's yes. What it does with the story of a feature that goes out is not set by the model: the product owner says.", "decided_by": "propose-answers (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:47:59Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what the plan play does when the slice changes after a plan exists", "found": "a second run makes no copies, nothing goes to the tracker before the yes, and the changed-slice rule is not set yet", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 20, "end": 22, "fingerprint": "sha256:324b2a6a4915a79c736df1bfad097680a096e52cb98e85b744965c7c5466b724", "text": "- A second run finds the plan, the epic and the stories that exist, and makes no copies.\n- Nothing goes to the tracker before the product owner's yes.\n- Thin: what the play does when the slice changes after a plan exists is not set yet.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 17, "end": 25, "text": "- The play runs after /shape-slice, on its own, and needs the slice to exist.\n- Each story carries the goal, the limits, the expectations and the Context guidance from its feature's ICE and its capability's ICE.\n- The play never writes a failure or recovery condition. The slice's hidden file belongs to /shape-slice (decision 6).\n- A second run finds the plan, the epic and the stories that exist, and makes no copies.\n- Nothing goes to the tracker before the product owner's yes.\n- Thin: what the play does when the slice changes after a plan exists is not set yet.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given a slice with three features, when the product owner runs /shape-plan and types yes, then one plan file, one epic and three stories exist."}}}, {"asked": "whether each feature of the slice must have one story", "found": "fails if a feature has no story or a second story is made for one feature", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 44, "end": 46, "fingerprint": "sha256:6d32cce6e8cb5a000490f23ce2b15407e86f9a5be47349137afb58551a0b0fb0", "text": "- Fails if: a feature of the slice has no story.\n- Fails if: a story or the plan file holds a failure condition or a recovery condition.\n- Fails if: a second run makes a second epic for the slice or a second story for one feature.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 41, "end": 48, "text": "- Limit: Write only the plan file, the epic and the stories. Never a failure condition, a recovery condition, the hidden file's failure or recovery lines, or the eval.\n- Limit: Each story holds the goal, the limits, the expectations and the Context guidance from its feature's ICE and that feature's capability's ICE.\n- Limit: Nothing goes to the tracker before the product owner's yes.\n- Fails if: a feature of the slice has no story.\n- Fails if: a story or the plan file holds a failure condition or a recovery condition.\n- Fails if: a second run makes a second epic for the slice or a second story for one feature.\n- Context: serves the product owner, who runs and tracks the plan, and the build play, which reads the stories; reads the slice from the spine and the ICE of each feature and its capability; writes .garura/project/plans/ and the tracker; out are the slice, the hidden file, the eval and the build. Not built yet (#818).\n- Checked by: the product owner runs /shape-plan 788 in Claude Code after /shape-slice and finds the plan file, one epic and one story for each feature, with no failure line in any story."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261025-017", "issue": 866, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In what form must the eval play write the eval of a slice, so that a person can run it from the outside?", "answer": "The eval is written in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). For each goal and expectation of the stories, and each failure condition of the slice's hidden file, it holds one check run from the outside on the slice's surface (for Garura often a run of the play on a test project), or a note that it cannot be tested yet. The layout of the file itself is not set by the model: the product owner says.", "decided_by": "propose-answers (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-25T06:47:59Z", "trace": [{"asked": "where the eval goes and whether its format is set", "found": "one eval in the plan's evals folder; the format is not set yet", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 11, "end": 13, "fingerprint": "sha256:b93cde941566d22f8052938724f9ccd125579b6b69cb933287c3d514fd7bf65d", "text": "- Out: one eval for the business intent in `.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/`.\n- Out (when needed): a handoff plan, which never names a failure condition, its id or its check.\n- Thin: the format of the eval and of the handoff plan is not set yet.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 16, "text": "## Inputs / Outputs\n- In: the epic of the slice, with its feature-to-story map, and its stories. The map joins each hidden-file entry (by its feature) to its story (ontology v11, Q36).\n- In: the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md) from the plan's evals folder.\n- Out: one eval for the business intent in `.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/`.\n- Out (when needed): a handoff plan, which never names a failure condition, its id or its check.\n- Thin: the format of the eval and of the handoff plan is not set yet.\n\n## Rules & behavior\n- The play runs after /shape-plan, on its own."}}}, {"asked": "how the eval checks", "found": "from the outside on the slice's surface, often a play on a test project; says when it cannot test a line yet", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 18, "end": 20, "fingerprint": "sha256:a328b9382c241adfa7d50c22485235986fdbe38e98a1f8562ebeb8df3e7b2c5c", "text": "- The eval checks from the outside, on the slice's surface. For Garura that surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project.\n- The running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (`guides/<slug>.md`).\n- When the eval cannot test a goal, an expectation or a failure condition yet, it says so.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 15, "end": 23, "text": "## Rules & behavior\n- The play runs after /shape-plan, on its own.\n- It reads only the epic, its stories and the hidden file. It never reads an ICE page, the usage guide or the code.\n- The eval checks from the outside, on the slice's surface. For Garura that surface is often a play, so the eval runs the play on a test project.\n- The running eval reaches the slice only through its usage guide (`guides/<slug>.md`).\n- When the eval cannot test a goal, an expectation or a failure condition yet, it says so.\n- Until eval encryption (#828) exists, only a read rule keeps builders out of the evals folder.\n\n## Acceptance criteria"}}}, {"asked": "what each check must cover", "found": "each goal, expectation and failure condition has a check or a note that it cannot be tested yet", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 25, "end": 25, "fingerprint": "sha256:704c849e5b5d54f153dd6bb385408aa60295d4490f8bf82def0ee24f2b87850e", "text": "- Given the eval, when a person reads it, then each goal and expectation of the stories, and each failure condition of the hidden file, has a check or a note that it cannot be tested yet.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 22, "end": 28, "text": "\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given a plan with an epic and its stories, when the product owner runs /shape-eval, then the eval is in the plan's evals folder.\n- Given the eval, when a person reads it, then each goal and expectation of the stories, and each failure condition of the hidden file, has a check or a note that it cannot be tested yet.\n- Given the build plays, when a person reads their inputs, then none names the evals folder.\n\n## Out of scope"}}}], "from_update": null}], "problems": []}
